-- title:
--   Bounded repartitions are bounded adèles
-- statement:
--   Fix fields $K$ and $F$ with $F$ a $K$-algebra, a divisor $D$ of $F/K$ — that is, a finitely supported function from `Place K F` (the type of valuation subrings of $F$ that contain the image of $K$, are not all of $F$, and are principal ideal rings) to $\mathbb{Z}$ — and an element $\alpha$ of the subalgebra `repartitions K F`, the $F$-subalgebra of the product $\prod_v F$ generated by those families $(\beta_v)_v$ for which $\{v : v.\mathrm{adicValuation}(\beta_v) \not\le 1\}$ is finite. The assertion is the equivalence of two membership statements: $\alpha$ belongs to the $K$-submodule `repartitionsOf D` of `repartitions K F`, cut out by the condition that $v.\mathrm{adicValuation}(\alpha_v) \le \exp(D_v)$ in $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$ for every place $v$, if and only if the underlying family $(\alpha_v)_v : \mathrm{Place}\,K\,F \to F$ belongs to the $K$-submodule `adeleBdd D` of $\prod_v F$, cut out by the very same inequality $v.\mathrm{adicValuation}(\alpha_v) \le \exp(D_v)$ for all $v$. Here $v.\mathrm{adicValuation}$ is the $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$-valued valuation attached to the height-one prime of the valuation subring $v$. No hypotheses beyond the field and algebra structures are imposed.
--
--   This identifies the two carriers used for the space $\mathbb{A}(D)$ of adèles bounded by a divisor: the one formed inside the repartition algebra of $F/K$ and the one formed inside the full product over places. It serves as the bridge between the two constructions, and is used in the computation of the adèle-space quotient as $H^1$ and in the finiteness of $H^1$ once the genus bound is attained.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_mem_repartitionsOf_iff_coe_mem_adeleBdd.lean

